#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287132 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e4bb90c5-2794-5657-8f0b-45eb64873e03" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given One Real Root, Two Complex Roots, and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c7f5f7d-ab42-5e39-bd72-118bed825a7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287134} {:answer/id #uuid "497b4193-bcb6-5dab-9680-70324e0a5e8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}+20x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287135} {:answer/id #uuid "3691e60a-f7c0-54b5-bd66-fe6cc8dab2d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+5x+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287136} {:answer/id #uuid "740d637a-c5ac-5cca-a9eb-04a6ad99f7a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}+12x+16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287137} {:answer/id #uuid "c427d897-a168-500f-909f-e5d5e7c62856" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+8x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287138}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "497b4193-bcb6-5dab-9680-70324e0a5e8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}+20x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287135} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d83d40e-262c-5dfe-acc8-334b2c95e9a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287133}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "30520f93-e92c-5fa8-bb5e-0a9ccde3033e" :question/math-academy-id "q-104478" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005293/assets/8d940d158c631143a1fe7652a4fb83bf2f67f3fd4bbdbbc4a33643bd282b5028.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of the cubic polynomial $f(x).$ Find $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $4.$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=0$ and ${x}_{2,3}=-1\\pm 2\\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=4.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =4(x-0)(x-(-1+2\\text{i}))(x-(-1-2\\text{i})) \\\\  & =4x(x-(-1+2\\text{i}))(x-(-1-2\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x(x-(-1+2\\text{i}))(x-(-1-2\\text{i})) & = \\\\ 4x({x}^{2}-x(-1-2\\text{i})-x(-1+2\\text{i})+(-1+2\\text{i})(-1-2\\text{i})) & = \\\\ 4x({x}^{2}+2x+5) & = \\\\ 4{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}+20x & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=4{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}+20x.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287139 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "517f2054-008e-54eb-89dd-5f0a09e1f881" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given Three Real Roots and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27e78b09-c56d-5859-b1a3-a04022b0e24d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+32x-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287141} {:answer/id #uuid "dfc34472-7c66-587f-8c25-f275ec9452d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-32x-40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287142} {:answer/id #uuid "a7de367a-7e35-5907-8632-6d394448c9cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}-16x-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287143} {:answer/id #uuid "5bc08d13-1fc6-5d2b-a481-c867d35e6ceb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}-32x-40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287144} {:answer/id #uuid "462ac7b0-1ecb-531e-9bcf-db07cc13beae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-16x-35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287145}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dfc34472-7c66-587f-8c25-f275ec9452d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-32x-40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287142} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b4c696e-5012-5f5d-8cfd-6336391f1335" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287140}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cf0a857f-eb4a-58c2-829d-65dd64e57db8" :question/math-academy-id "q-107538" :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=-2,{x}_{3}=5,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $2.$ Find $P(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=-2$ and ${x}_{3}=5,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =2(x-(-2))(x-(-2))(x-5) \\\\  & =2(x+2)(x+2)(x-5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x+2)(x+2)(x-5) & =2({x}^{2}+4x+4)(x-5) \\\\  & =2({x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-5{x}^{2}+4x-20x-20) \\\\  & =2({x}^{3}-{x}^{2}-16x-20) \\\\  & =2{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-32x-40.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=2{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-32x-40.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287146 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "517f2054-008e-54eb-89dd-5f0a09e1f881" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given Three Real Roots and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f1b89a3b-2d8d-5de7-85e1-8a77d1284d8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287148}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f1b89a3b-2d8d-5de7-85e1-8a77d1284d8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287148} :answer-field/id #uuid "08cc154c-cb06-5a68-8d1a-7f0da8e823a9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287147} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d8f0577-f991-5218-9efc-9114f72fabfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287150}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d8f0577-f991-5218-9efc-9114f72fabfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287150} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8825049-8f9c-5f2c-b7d5-5208575afe59" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287149} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c48b2e8-7314-5080-8d45-fe5f4d23fde6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287152}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2c48b2e8-7314-5080-8d45-fe5f4d23fde6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287152} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c38b985-1389-54b8-adaf-44b34b9e6d94" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287151} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39623404-05a6-5390-8ec7-19f4b902184a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "90" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287154}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39623404-05a6-5390-8ec7-19f4b902184a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "90" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287154} :answer-field/id #uuid "815d2405-11cc-530b-909d-b35eaa7f50f2" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287153}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "46e23247-a138-55b5-8a0b-f43cda1d72d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-316626" :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=3,{x}_{3}=-2,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $5.$ Find $P(x).$\n\n$P(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,-$\n{{field-2}}${x}^{2}\\,-$\n{{field-3}}$x\\,+$\n{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=3,$ ${x}_{2}=3,$ and ${x}_{3}=-2,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=5,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =5(x-3)(x-3)(x-(-2)) \\\\  & =5(x-3)(x-3)(x+2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(x-3)(x-3)(x+2) & =5({x}^{2}-6x+9)(x+2) \\\\  & =5({x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-6{x}^{2}-12x+9x+18) \\\\  & =5({x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-3x+18) \\\\  & =5{x}^{3}-20{x}^{2}-15x+90.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=5{x}^{3}-20{x}^{2}-15x+90.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287155 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e4bb90c5-2794-5657-8f0b-45eb64873e03" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given One Real Root, Two Complex Roots, and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42bcd0c6-e177-5a0f-85ea-69191d88baa4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287157} {:answer/id #uuid "d0af8636-e199-5f7e-963a-6d41a50ed82d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287158}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42bcd0c6-e177-5a0f-85ea-69191d88baa4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287157} :answer-field/id #uuid "044ee52f-366e-59b0-8a72-1174479473a5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287156} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "756e601c-d73e-5119-8659-eeddcc739688" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287160}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "756e601c-d73e-5119-8659-eeddcc739688" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287160} :answer-field/id #uuid "475afaea-e62c-59e3-85c6-aa749257fd3e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287159} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb9082de-24d6-5ed3-83cb-29d8d5a412f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287162}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb9082de-24d6-5ed3-83cb-29d8d5a412f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287162} :answer-field/id #uuid "a20ca450-bba3-56c6-8f45-a00258cd77f3" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287161} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5b4665f-26b1-500e-8eea-78107290637c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "96" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287164}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a5b4665f-26b1-500e-8eea-78107290637c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "96" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287164} :answer-field/id #uuid "89f8afbc-60ce-5415-98ba-0207af04e946" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287163}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e84c17cd-0769-5299-a213-2af1da95b80b" :question/math-academy-id "q-316646" :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-2,{x}_{2,3}=\\pm 4\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $3.$ Find $f(x).$\n\n$f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,+$\n{{field-2}}${x}^{2}\\,+$\n{{field-3}}$x\\,+$\n{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "Since $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-2$ and ${x}_{2,3}=\\pm 4\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=3,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =3(x-(-2))(x-4\\text{i})(x-(-4\\text{i})) \\\\  & =3(x+2)(x-4\\text{i})(x+4\\text{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(x+2)(x-4\\text{i})(x+4\\text{i}) & = \\\\ 3(x+2)({x}^{2}-(4\\text{i})^{2}) & = \\\\ 3(x+2)({x}^{2}+16) & = \\\\ 3({x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+16x+32) & = \\\\ 3{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+48x+96 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=3{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+48x+96.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287165 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e4bb90c5-2794-5657-8f0b-45eb64873e03" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given One Real Root, Two Complex Roots, and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dab081ae-c3cb-50ee-ab7f-c0181b635b35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287167}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dab081ae-c3cb-50ee-ab7f-c0181b635b35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287167} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebf2970d-a965-5a9a-bb39-97f965d999ec" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287166} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b78ff806-5fa0-53b5-a2ae-beae6c10d44e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287169}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b78ff806-5fa0-53b5-a2ae-beae6c10d44e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287169} :answer-field/id #uuid "600996a6-d8d3-56da-912f-92023b23a4ef" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287168} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8b3938a-8e06-501b-bfdc-2334df9082c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287171}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a8b3938a-8e06-501b-bfdc-2334df9082c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287171} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d563a17-24a0-5fd5-be9b-7e768a713e82" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287170} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7942cf66-c4b5-58c8-b998-5be48d0366ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "216" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287173}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7942cf66-c4b5-58c8-b998-5be48d0366ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "216" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287173} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6dd5b35-9b9d-5e95-ae71-5175f3d62bc5" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287172}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f053ef04-442b-5bfb-bbfc-7c45f7d96fed" :question/math-academy-id "q-316707" :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=6,\\,{x}_{2,3}=\\pm 3\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $-4.$ Find $f(x).$\n\n$f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,+$\n{{field-2}}${x}^{2}\\,-$\n{{field-3}}$x\\,+$\n{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "Since $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=6$ and ${x}_{2,3}=\\pm 3\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=-4,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =-4(x-6)(x-3\\text{i})(x-(-3\\text{i})) \\\\  & =-4(x-6)(x-3\\text{i})(x+3\\text{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4(x-6)(x-3\\text{i})(x+3\\text{i}) & = \\\\ -4(x-6)({x}^{2}-x(-3\\text{i})-x(3\\text{i})+(3\\text{i})(-3\\text{i})) & = \\\\ -4(x-6)({x}^{2}+9) & = \\\\ -4({x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+9x-54) & = \\\\ -4{x}^{3}+24{x}^{2}-36x+216.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=-4{x}^{3}+24{x}^{2}-36x+216.$"}]}
